From: Vyron Code D-11 local hardening (VYRON_CODE_D11_FINAL_EPHEMERAL_DIAGNOSTICS_PATCH, incremental)
Applies to: NousResearch/hermes-agent, installed local copy, version 0.21.0.

OPTIONAL, NOT APPLIED BY THIS TOOLING. This environment's permission system refuses every real
write to Hermes's installed source, so this patch was never applied here - only generated and
dry-run verified (`git apply --check`) against the real installed files. The user applies it
themselves.

CONTEXT: patch 0001 (`agent._persist_disabled = True`) is confirmed present and correct. Patch
0002 was intended to close two further gaps in the same installed source - a request-dump file
(`agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py::dump_api_request_debug`) and three log lines that carry prompt/
error content (`agent/turn_context.py`, `agent/turn_recovery.py`) - but a direct read-back of the
installed source shows NONE of patch 0002's four hunks are present, including the
`agent_runtime_helpers.py` one. This patch (0003) covers only the two files explicitly requested
this round - `agent/turn_context.py` and `agent/turn_recovery.py` - using the exact hunks from
0002 for those two files, with the placeholder text changed to the fixed strings specified for
this round. The `agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py` hunk from patch 0002 is untouched here and still
needs to be applied separately (0002 itself is unchanged and already dry-run-verified) - it is
not duplicated into this file, since scope was explicitly limited to `turn_context.py` and
`turn_recovery.py` only.

WHAT IT DOES (three hunks, two files):

  1. `agent/turn_context.py` - the per-turn `logger.info("conversation turn: ... msg=%r", ...)`
     line that runs on every turn (success or failure) and, until now, always included an 80-char
     preview of the user's actual message text. When the calling agent has
     `_persist_disabled = True`, the preview is replaced with the fixed placeholder
     `[ephemeral task content suppressed]`; the rest of the line (session/model/provider/
     platform/history length) is unchanged, so operational log lines for ordinary,
     non-ephemeral agents are completely unaffected.

  2. `agent/turn_recovery.py`, non-retryable-client-error path (~line 703) - the
     `logger.error("... Non-retryable client error: %s", ...)` line, which logs the raw provider
     exception (`api_error`) - a value that can, for some provider failure modes, itself echo
     back request content. When `_persist_disabled` is set, this is replaced with the fixed
     placeholder `[ephemeral API error detail suppressed]`; the rest of the line (the
     `agent.log_prefix` tag) is unchanged.

  3. `agent/turn_recovery.py`, retry-attempt warning (~line 871) - the
     `logger.warning("API call failed ... summary=%s", ...)` line, which logs `_error_summary`
     (a summarized form of the same provider error/response text). When `_persist_disabled` is
     set, this is replaced with the same fixed placeholder `[ephemeral API error detail
     suppressed]`; retry count, exception type, and `agent._client_log_context()` (provider/
     model/thread context) are unchanged, so error-rate monitoring for ordinary agents keeps
     working exactly as before.

WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TOUCH:

  - `agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py::dump_api_request_debug` - covered by patch 0002, not
    duplicated here.
  - The `[session_id]` tag every Hermes log line carries (via the logging session-context filter
    set up in `set_session_context()`), used by `hermes logs` to group lines per run. It is
    generic logging infrastructure that applies to every platform and every agent, not something
    tied to a specific log line's content, and it is an opaque correlator, not task content -
    de-scoping it keeps this patch to the narrowest change that actually stops task/response/
    error *content* from landing on disk.
  - Any non-`api_server` platform, or any `api_server` agent that does NOT have
    `_persist_disabled = True` set (every guard is conditional on that exact flag).

HOW TO APPLY (PowerShell, run as the same user who owns the Hermes installation):
  1. Back up first:
       $ts = Get-Date -Format "yyyyMMdd_HHmmss"
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_context.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_context.py.vyron-pre-0003-patch-$ts.bak"
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_recovery.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_recovery.py.vyron-pre-0003-patch-$ts.bak"
  2. From this repository root:
       git apply --directory="$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent" hermes-patches/0003-api-server-ephemeral-log-redaction.patch
     (or, if PowerShell's own path handling causes `git apply` to complain, `cd` directly into
     `$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent` first - which is itself a git repository - and run
     `git apply "D:\Vyron Code\hermes-patches\0003-api-server-ephemeral-log-redaction.patch"`
     from there instead, with no `--directory` flag.)
  3. Restart Hermes: stop any running `hermes gateway run`, then start it again.

VERIFY IT ACTUALLY APPLIED (do this - a silent `git apply` failure is easy to miss):
       Select-String -Path "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_context.py" -Pattern "VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH"
       Select-String -Path "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\agent\turn_recovery.py" -Pattern "VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH"
     Each command should print at least one matching line. If either prints nothing, the patch
     did not apply and Hermes is still running the unpatched source.

HOW TO ROLL BACK:
  Restore the two `.bak` files created in step 1 over their originals, then restart Hermes.

